  "result": "I fixed it. The bug was in `IntRange._clamp` (`src/click/types.py:754`): when a bound was open (`min_open` or `max_open`), clamping moved the value away from the allowed range instead of into it. For example, `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turned `-10` into `-1`, when it should be `1`. The max side had the same problem: `10` became `6` instead of `4`.\n\nThe fix is a one-character change from `bound - dir` to `bound + dir`, so the value now steps one integer inside the open bound. Clamping to closed bounds wasn't affected.\n\nI also added two regression cases to `tests/test_types.py`, one for an open min and one for an open max. `tests/test_types.py` passes (43 passed, 2 skipped), as do the other range-related tests in the suite. I haven't run the full test suite.",
